<title>INDIA: Foreign buying buoys Delhi shares in early trade.</title>
<headline>Foreign buying buoys Delhi shares in early trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Selective buying by foreign institutional investors in index-linked stocks pushed up share prices on the Delhi Stock Exchange on Monday, brokers said.</p>
<p>The bourse's benchmark index was 2.53 points higher at 806.88 after 30 minutes of trade.</p>
